SIM-04: document leak expansion as sq mm per metre of head

leakage.c reads the [LEAKAGE] expansion rate (EN_LEAK_EXPAN) as sq mm
per metre of pressure head in both unit systems, the design stated in
issue #899 and implemented by PR #901. The [LEAKAGE] page and the enum
comment say per unit of head (ft or m), so a US user who follows them
gets 0.3048 times the intended variable-area leakage. Correct the two
documentation strings; the code does not change.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-04_fix.patch

diff --git a/doc/toolkit-input.dox b/doc/toolkit-input.dox
index 93031c9..6f2c208 100644
--- a/doc/toolkit-input.dox
+++ b/doc/toolkit-input.dox
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@ __Format:__
 A line for each pipe subject to leaking that contains:
 - Pipe ID label
 - the average combined area of leakage-generating cracks per 100 units of pipe length (in ft or m). This area is expressed in units of square mm regardless of the choice of model flow units.
-- the expansion in the average combined area of leakage-generating cracks as a function of the pressure head (in ft or m). This is the derivative of the area with respect to the pressure head, and is expressed in units of sq. mm per unit of modeled pressure head (in ft or m)
+- the expansion in the average combined area of leakage-generating cracks as a function of the pressure head, per 100 units of pipe length (in ft or m). This is the derivative of the area with respect to the pressure head, and is expressed in units of sq. mm per m of pressure head regardless of the choice of model flow units.
 
 __Remarks__
 1. This section is optional.
